────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHAT THESE LICENCES DO NOT COVER
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
This repository describes 116 design systems that belong to other people. The
two licences above cover *this repository's own work* — the measurements, the
analysis, the wording, the tooling. They do not and cannot relicense anything
upstream.

1. Token values are facts. Numbers such as "40px" or "#0d1117" are measurements
   of what a system does, and facts are not copyrightable. Every claim records
   the repository and the version or commit it was read from, so an upstream
   licence can always be checked at the source. Each entry's `license:` field
   carries what that system declares; `design-systems/UNVERIFIED.md` lists the
   ones that declare nothing.

2. No upstream prose is reproduced. The corpus rule is summarise and link, never
   copy. If you find verbatim third-party prose here, it is a defect — please
   open an issue.

3. No third-party assets are stored. Organisation logos on the website are the
   organisation's own GitHub avatar, requested by the reader's browser at view
   time. Nothing is vendored, cached or redistributed.

4. Trade marks are not licensed. Product and organisation names appear
   nominatively, to say which system was measured.

5. Pretendard, the website's typeface, is under SIL OFL-1.1 and is loaded from
   jsDelivr rather than bundled here.

If you own one of the systems described here and something is wrong — a
misreading, a licence conflict, or an entry you would rather not have — open an
issue and it will be corrected or removed.
